# Documentation policy.
#
# This repository is public, so the default was "private unless proven safe" and
# whole directories were excluded. That put the operational runbooks, the
# incident records and the monitoring documentation - all of which the
# certification reports cite - somewhere a reader cannot reach, and the reports
# had to say so.
#
# The excluded tree was audited on 3 September 2026 for credentials, tokens,
# connection strings, live hostnames, IP addresses, bucket names and personal
# data. One finding: a Cloudflare Message-ID in the E4 dossier, since redacted.
# Everything else was clean, so the default is inverted: versioned unless there
# is a reason.
#
# What stays out, and why:
#   notebook-*.md          working notes, superseded by the architecture docs
#   diagrams/final/        exported binaries, regenerated from the .dot sources
#   privacy-rgpd.md        working draft; the register is the versioned record
#   *_superseded ADRs      already marked superseded in their filenames
#   evaluation-word/       Word drafts of the reports plus a third-party
#                          institutional brochure - drafts are not the
#                          submission, and the brochure is not ours to publish
#   screenshots/           unreviewed captures; a dashboard screenshot can
#                          carry addresses, tokens or customer data
docs/architecture/notebook-*.md
docs/architecture/diagrams/final/
docs/architecture/privacy-rgpd.md
docs/architecture/diagrams/*.dot
docs/adr/0001-post-delivery-gmail.md
docs/adr/0006-scope-selection-gmail.md
docs/certification/evaluation-word/
docs/certification/screenshots/
docs/**/*.docx
docs/**/*.pdf
docs/adr/0007-idempotency-pubsub-history.md
docs/raw_sources/
docs/simplon/
docs/model/
docs/brand/*.md
docs/deployment/
docs/email-intercept.md
deploy/hetzner/*.md
deploy/nginx/ssl/*.md
deploy/README.md
tasks/
scratch/

research/

